58" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/state.json" "file_sha256" "2577dbc99907a5411ab3f521f826b43bb8ea341f7d7830c1712e1f103fbd9d7b" "basis" 1395 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set and \n${v}_{1}={v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}-{v}_{4},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set\n- ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$\n- ${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/state.json" "file_sha256" "2577dbc99907a5411ab3f521f826b43bb8ea341f7d7830c1712e1f103fbd9d7b" "basis" 1395 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since ${v}_{1}={v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}-{v}_{4},$ we have that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot {v}_{1}+(-1)\\cdot {v}_{2}+(-5)\\cdot {v}_{3}+1\\cdot {v}_{4}=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution and the set ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent by definition.\n\n- Statement II is false.  Since ${v}_{1}={v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}-{v}_{4},$ the equation ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${v}_{1}={v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}-{v}_{4},$ we have that\n\n$$\n{v}_{4}={v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}-{v}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThat is, ${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/state.json" "file_sha256" "2577dbc99907a5411ab3f521f826b43bb8ea341f7d7830c1712e1f103fbd9d7b" "basis" 1395 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d71977646c1e36c70f1fffe1edfd6b8373aa65a6561f5312a3b6a497291d13fc" "basis" 1395 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/state.json" "file_sha256" "2577dbc99907a5411ab3f521f826b43bb8ea341f7d7830c1712e1f103fbd9d7b" "basis" 1395 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/state.json" "file_sha256" "2577dbc99907a5411ab3f521f826b43bb8ea341f7d7830c1712e1f103fbd9d7b" "basis" 1395 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/state.json" "file_sha256" "2577dbc99907a5411ab3f521f826b43bb8ea341f7d7830c1712e1f103fbd9d7b" "basis" 1395 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/state.json" "file_sha256" "2577dbc99907a5411ab3f521f826b43bb8ea341f7d7830c1712e1f103fbd9d7b" "basis" 1395 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/state.json" "file_sha256" "2577dbc99907a5411ab3f521f826b43bb8ea341f7d7830c1712e1f103fbd9d7b" "basis" 1395 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-43786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/state.json" "file_sha256" "2577dbc99907a5411ab3f521f826b43bb8ea341f7d7830c1712e1f103fbd9d7b" "basis" 1395 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-107044" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{3},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3}}$ is linearly  independent\n- ${0,{v}_{1},-{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent\n- ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/state.json" "file_sha256" "2577dbc99907a5411ab3f521f826b43bb8ea341f7d7830c1712e1f103fbd9d7b" "basis" 1395 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-107044" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}({v}_{1}-{v}_{3})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2}-{v}_{3}) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}-({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot {v}_{1}+0\\cdot (-{v}_{2})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}0+{x}_{2}{v}_{1}+{x}_{3}(-{v}_{2})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${0,{v}_{1},-{v}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. In general, any set containing the zero vector is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n1\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+1\\cdot ({v}_{2}-{v}_{1})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$  is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/state.json" "file_sha256" "2577dbc99907a5411ab3f521f826b43bb8ea341f7d7830c1712e1f103fbd9d7b" "basis" 1395 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-107044" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d71977646c1e36c70f1fffe1edfd6b8373aa65a6561f5312a3b6a497291d13fc" "basis" 1395 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-107044" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/state.json" "file_sha256" "2577dbc99907a5411ab3f521f826b43bb8ea341f7d7830c1712e1f103fbd9d7b" "basis" 1395 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039921/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q